oai_dc:dc.dc:description:
There are very few records of the Cicadabird Coracina tenuirostris from Western&nbsp;Australia. Here I report observations of an adult male and a female-type Cicadabird along&nbsp;the Upper Mitchell River, in the north-west of the Kimberley region of Western Australia,&nbsp;on 13 May 2010. The environment was a wide and well-timbered river bed running through&nbsp;open savanna. Other records of the species in Western Australia are reviewed. Published&nbsp;records of 10 specimens claimed to be of this species, from the Fitzroy River and Napier&nbsp;Broome Bay, appear not to be of the Cicadabird. The species appears to be absent from&nbsp;the extreme north-eastern Kimberley.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
